<newsitem itemid="114895" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Waste Management Intnl Q3 pretax rises.</title>
<headline>Waste Management Intnl Q3 pretax rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>three months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.0		    vs 6.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     42.8		   vs 39.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   309.7		  vs 299.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Waste Management International Plc provides solid and hazardous waste management services.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 44.5		   vs 44.3</p>
<p> Interest income	  1.8		    vs 2.4</p>
<p> Interest expense	 9.9		    vs 13.3</p>
<p> Tax			  11.0		   vs 10.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  31.7		   vs 29.3</p>
<p> Attributable	     26.4		   vs 24.5</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it has revised its full year cash flow projection to 50 million stg from 70 million because of events in Argentina, where the Buenos Aires municipal government has frozen and delayed payments to suppliers. Difficult solid waste trading continued to adversely affect results in Germany. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
